  "design": "Authority manifests use version 3 and retain the complete authority head in the same immutable generation record. Ordinary manifests keep version 2 and omit the new field. Finite permission receipts renew independently against the committed head.",
  "observations": [
    "The head must match the generation ID and payload digest. Duplicate and case-variant JSON fields cannot replace the binding.",
    "Memory, filesystem, and the conditional object adapter commit the required permission revision with the generation under the existing compare-and-swap contract.",
    "An injected filesystem failure before head publication preserves the prior catalog and permission revision after reopen. Retrying publishes the complete new pair."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The object adapter uses the existing in-memory ObjectBackend fixture. This does not qualify an external object service.",
    "Issuer revision selection, runtime authority policy, retained permission state, receipt issuance, and Starport admission remain incomplete.",
    "All eight CSP4 acceptance subcases remain UNVERIFIED. No task completion or publication credit."
  ]
